{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>From the people.</b> And not from the priests (Sifrei; Ḥulin 132)." "<b>Whether ox or sheep.</b> Excludes undomesticated animals." "<b>The stomach.</b> From the joint of the foreleg up to the palm of the hand, which is called אשפלד\"ון (Ḥulin 134)." "<b>The cheeks.</b> With the tongue. Those who expound verses by analogy used to say: the arm corresponds to 'hand,' as it says (Numbers 25) ״וַיִּקַּח רֹמַח בְּיָדוֹ״; the cheeks correspond to 'prayer,' as it says (Psalms 106) ״וַיַּעֲמֹד פִּנְחָס וַיְפַלֵּל״; and הַקֵּבָה corresponds to ״הָאִשָּׁה אֶל קֳבָתָהּ״ (Numbers 25)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {2 "אשפלד\"ון is an Old French anatomical term in Hebrew script; the citation Ḥulin 134 locates the passage in tractate Ḥullin."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:35.192954228Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}